claim.claim-text:
1. A control device for a hybrid vehicle which comprises an engine (1) as a power source for running the vehicle and a motor/generator (2), comprising: 
a high-voltage battery (11) which functions as a power source for the motor/generator (2); 
a low-voltage battery (14) for vehicle-mounted electrical loads which has a lower voltage than the high-voltage battery (11); 
an inverter (12) for controlling the motor/generator (2); 
a sensor (18,19) which detects a condition of the high-voltage battery (11); and 
a microprocessor (16) which is programmed to: 
compute a state of charge (SOC) of the high-voltage battery (11) based on the condition of the high-voltage battery (11); 
compute a degree of deterioration of the high-voltage battery (11) based on the condition of the high-voltage battery (11); 
control a current generated by the motor/generator (2) so that the SOC of the high-voltage battery (11) coincides with a target SOC; and 
vary the target SOC according to the degree of deterioration of the high-voltage battery (11).

7. The control device as defined in claim 1, wherein the microprocessor (16) is further programmed to: 
compute a target charging current to the high-voltage battery (11) according to the SOC of the high-voltage battery (11); 
compute an electrical load current for vehicle-mounted electrical loads; 
compute a target generated current generated by the motor/generator (2) by adding the target charging current and the electrical load current; and 
control a target torque which is supplied to the motor/generator (2) so that the current generated by the motor/generator (2) is equal to the target generated current.

9. A control device for a hybrid vehicle which comprises an engine (1) as a power source for running the vehicle and a motor/generator (2), comprising; 
a high-voltage battery (11) which functions as a power source of the motor/generator (2); 
a low-voltage battery (14) for vehicle-mounted electrical loads which has a lower voltage than the high-voltage battery (11); 
an inverter (12) for controlling the motor/generator (2); 
a sensor (18,19) which detects a condition of the high-voltage battery (11); 
a sensor (31) which detects a rotation speed of the engine (1); 
a sensor (34) which detects a vehicle speed; 
a sensor (35) which detects depression of an accelerator pedal; 
a sensor (36) which detects depression of a brake pedal; and 
a microprocessor (16) programmed to: 
compute a state of charge (SOC) of the high-voltage battery (11) based on the condition of the high-voltage battery (11); 
determine whether or not the vehicle is brought to a temporary halt with the engine running at idle speed, based on the rotation speed of the engine, the vehicle speed, the depression of the accelerator pedal, and the depression of the brake pedal; and 
stop the engine (1) when the SOC of the high-voltage battery (11) is greater than or equal to a threshold value and when the vehicle is brought to the temporary halt with the engine running at the idle speed.

20. A control device for a hybrid vehicle which comprises an engine (1) as a power source for running the vehicle and a motor/generator (2), comprising: 
a high-voltage battery (11) which functions as a power source for the motor/generator (2); 
a low-voltage battery (14) for vehicle-mounted electrical loads which has a lower voltage than the high-voltage battery (11); 
means (12) for controlling the motor/generator (2); 
means (18,19) for detecting a condition of the high-voltage battery (11); 
means for computing a state of charge (SOC) of the high-voltage battery (11) based on the condition of the high-voltage battery (11); 
means for computing a degree of deterioration of the high-voltage battery (11) based on the condition of the high-voltage battery (11); 
means for controlling a current generated by the motor/generator (2) so that the SOC of the high-voltage battery (11) coincides with a target SOC; and 
means for varying the target SOC according to the degree of deterioration of the high-voltage battery (11).
